	"notice": "Use USB MIDI or a DIN MIDI interface. Match the MIDI channel and enable the required MIDI transmit/receive settings. Original JP-08, not JUPITER-08. Use normal instrument mode and current firmware for panel CC. Lower-part control changes use the channel above the configured upper-part channel (wrapping after 16).  GUI controls generate MIDI into the chain; route that chain to a MIDI output to control the hardware. DIN devices normally appear under the MIDI interface name, so select the profile manually. Unmapped physical buttons and switches have stable SVG IDs for future bindings. Positions are schematic. Note surfaces use virtual defaults; use MIDI learn to match the hardware octave or configuration.",
